diff --git a/doc/user/ospfd.rst b/doc/user/ospfd.rst
index 04d0c85d58..7df6e82046 100644
--- a/doc/user/ospfd.rst
+++ b/doc/user/ospfd.rst
@@ -271,6 +271,34 @@ To start OSPF process you have to specify the OSPF router.
    number of second remaining till on-startup or on-shutdown ends, can be
    viewed with the :clicmd:`show ip ospf` command.
 
+.. clicmd:: max-lsa (1-4294967294) [threshold (1-100)] [warning-only] [ignore-time (30-3600)] [ignore-count (1-32)] [reset-time (60-86400)]
+
+   Limit the number of LSAs of other routers in the link-state databases of
+   the instance (the self-originated LSAs do not count), so that a wrong
+   redistribution elsewhere in the domain cannot run this router out of
+   memory. Each LSA costs about 1.5 KiB in *ospfd*, and a route about 0.6
+   KiB in *zebra*; a flood of 175 000 type-5 LSAs reaches a router in one
+   second.
+
+   At ``threshold`` percent of the limit (default 75) a warning is logged.
+   Above the limit the instance goes down for ``ignore-time`` seconds (default
+   300): all interfaces go down, so every adjacency drops, and the learned
+   LSAs are discarded. The databases of the area stay consistent, as no
+   router computes a path through this one without adjacencies. The instance
+   then comes up again; after ``ignore-count`` (default 5) such periods it
+   stays down until :clicmd:`clear ip ospf max-lsa`. ``reset-time`` seconds
+   (default 600) up without exceeding the limit reset the count of periods.
+   With ``warning-only`` the instance only logs above the limit.
+
+   The state, the count and the time left are shown by :clicmd:`show ip ospf`
+   (``lsaOtherRoutersCounter`` and ``maxLsa`` in its JSON).
+
+   A limit close to the normal size of the database takes the router off the
+   network on normal growth, and the same limit on every router takes them
+   all down together: leave room. The memory taken by a flood is not given
+   back to the system after the LSAs are discarded, so the limit bounds the
+   peak.
+
 .. clicmd:: auto-cost reference-bandwidth (1-4294967)
 
 
@@ -345,6 +373,12 @@ To start OSPF process you have to specify the OSPF router.
    in router-id and if user wants the router-id change to take effect, user can
    use this cli instead of restarting the ospfd daemon.
 
+.. clicmd:: clear ip ospf [(1-65535)] max-lsa
+
+   Leave the ignore or isolated state of :clicmd:`max-lsa` now and reset the
+   count of ignore periods: the interfaces come up again. Fix what floods the
+   LSAs first, or the instance goes down again.
+
